    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0009:0001",
      "blockId": "paragraph:discussion:0009",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "The following Metal code demonstrates how to replicate the emissive behavior of [`PhysicallyBasedMaterial`](physicallybasedmaterial.md) in your surface shader code:",
      "normalizedSource": "The following Metal code demonstrates how to replicate the emissive behavior of [`PhysicallyBasedMaterial`](physicallybasedmaterial.md) in your surface shader code:",
      "sourceHash": "68e587b11b54828d6f0f34ff6ce33aac10fb066af205203da9b91a26224c833f",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "With custom materials, `color` and `texture` are available as inputs in your surface shader, but your surface shader must call `params.surface().set_emissive_color()`, otherwise RealityKit renders no light emission.",
      "contextAfter": "```swift\n    // Retrieve the emissive color tint from the CustomMaterial.\n    half3 emissiveColorTint = (half3)params.material_constants()\n                              .emissive_color_tint();\n\n    // Retrieve the primary texture coordinates.\n    float2 uv = params.geometry().uv0();\n\n    // Flip the UV coordinate’s y-axis. You only need to do this\n    // for models you load from USDZ or .reality files.\n    uv.y = 1.0 - uv.y;\n\n    auto tex = params.textures();\n    half3 color = (half3)tex.emissive_color()\n                  .sample(textureSampler, uv).rgb;\n\n    // Multiply the tint and the sampled value from the texture,\n    // and assign the result to the shader's emissive color\n    // property.\n    color *= emissiveColorTint;\n    params.surface().set_emissive_color(color);\n```",
      "documentTitle": "init(color:texture:)",
      "framework": "RealityKit",
      "ko": "",
      "status": "failed",
      "reviewed": false,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:code:discussion:0010:0001",
      "blockId": "code:discussion:0010",
      "type": "preserve",
      "source": "```swift\n    // Retrieve the emissive color tint from the CustomMaterial.\n    half3 emissiveColorTint = (half3)params.material_constants()\n                              .emissive_color_tint();\n\n    // Retrieve the primary texture coordinates.\n    float2 uv = params.geometry().uv0();\n\n    // Flip the UV coordinate’s y-axis. You only need to do this\n    // for models you load from USDZ or .reality files.\n    uv.y = 1.0 - uv.y;\n\n    auto tex = params.textures();\n    half3 color = (half3)tex.emissive_color()\n                  .sample(textureSampler, uv).rgb;\n\n    // Multiply the tint and the sampled value from the texture,\n    // and assign the result to the shader's emissive color\n    // property.\n    color *= emissiveColorTint;\n    params.surface().set_emissive_color(color);\n```",
      "normalizedSource": "```swift // Retrieve the emissive color tint from the CustomMaterial. half3 emissiveColorTint = (half3)params.material_constants() .emissive_color_tint(); // Retrieve the primary texture coordinates. float2 uv = params.geometry().uv0(); // Flip the UV coordinate’s y-axis. You only need to do this // for models you load from USDZ or .reality files. uv.y = 1.0 - uv.y; auto tex = params.textures(); half3 color = (half3)tex.emissive_color() .sample(textureSampler, uv).rgb; // Multiply the tint and the sampled value from the texture, // and assign the result to the shader's emissive color // property. color *= emissiveColorTint; params.surface().set_emissive_color(color); ```",
      "sourceHash": "2a0e2021da8e8945f235668024f9531f8ed319f89e14e747cf77c5b29f4fc3b3",
      "translatable": false,
      "preserveReason": "code",
      "contextBefore": "The following Metal code demonstrates how to replicate the emissive behavior of [`PhysicallyBasedMaterial`](physicallybasedmaterial.md) in your surface shader code:",
      "contextAfter": "**Note**: Unlike [`PhysicallyBasedMaterial`](physicallybasedmaterial.md), [`CustomMaterial`](custommaterial.md) has no [`emissiveIntensity`](physicallybasedmaterial/emissiveintensity.md) value.",
      "documentTitle": "init(color:texture:)",
      "framework": "RealityKit",
      "ko": "```swift\n    // Retrieve the emissive color tint from the CustomMaterial.\n    half3 emissiveColorTint = (half3)params.material_constants()\n                              .emissive_color_tint();\n\n    // Retrieve the primary texture coordinates.\n    float2 uv = params.geometry().uv0();\n\n    // Flip the UV coordinate’s y-axis. You only need to do this\n    // for models you load from USDZ or .reality files.\n    uv.y = 1.0 - uv.y;\n\n    auto tex = params.textures();\n    half3 color = (half3)tex.emissive_color()\n                  .sample(textureSampler, uv).rgb;\n\n    // Multiply the tint and the sampled value from the texture,\n    // and assign the result to the shader's emissive color\n    // property.\n    color *= emissiveColorTint;\n    params.surface().set_emissive_color(color);\n```",
